## Behavior Pattern Analysis

### Pattern 1: Combat Priority System

Weapons use `<TargetPriority>` to establish attack preferences:

```xml
<TargetPriority type="Flying">10</TargetPriority>
<TargetPriority type="Infantry">7</TargetPriority>
<TargetPriority type="Building">1</TargetPriority>
```

**Common Priority Ladders:**
- Infantry > Ground Vehicles > Turrets > Buildings
- Aircraft > Everything else
- Painted targets (highest)

### Pattern 2: Cover System

Files with `<SquadMode>Cover</SquadMode>` support defensive positioning:
- `InCoverGrenade` vs `Grenade` actions show different ranges/accuracy
- Cover transitions create tactical depth

### Pattern 3: Transport Mechanics

Multi-action garrison/ungarrison sequences:
- HotDrop (immediate deployment)
- Teleport (map mechanics)
- Standard Garrison (slow)
- Ungarrison + animation chains

### Pattern 4: State Transitions

Only 4 files use explicit `<State>` definitions:
- `cov_inf_bruterider_01` - RamState (ramming mechanics)
- `cov_inf_lekgologoliath_01_mp` - RamState (melee rush)
- `cov_veh_locust_01` - RamState (vehicle charging)

### Pattern 5: Special Data Types

Some actions use `<SpecificData>` for unique mechanics:
- `RepairOther` - Drone/platform repairs
- `HQAnimTeleport` - Building teleportation
- `Drone` - Autonomous behavior
- `AnimDeliver` - Animation-locked delivery

